                    coach_r1_sharp:         `<strong>Sharp diagnosis.</strong> Thin liquidity raises transaction costs, high costs keep institutions away, weak demand depresses the multiple — and closing the 1.8-turn gap is worth ~€137M on €76M of EBITDA. That is the chain the whole re-rating runs on.`,
                    coach_r1_earnings:      `<strong>That is earnings tunnel vision.</strong> You can promise a better quarter, but the spread is still 65 bp and institutions still cannot build a position without moving the price against themselves. Earnings rose; the multiple did not. Value lives in the liquidity–governance chain, not the P&L alone.`,
                    coach_r1_macro:         `<strong>"It's the market, nothing to fix" is how the discount becomes permanent.</strong> Peers trade at 9.0x in the same tape; the gap is Lumiform-specific — a thin float and weak governance, both of which you can change.`,
